From: Shammah Chancellor <shammah.chancellor@notvalid.com>
Date: Mon, 19 Oct 2026 13:40:07 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] test(v2): pin transaction identities, genesis and coin
 encodings before the bridge

The legacy bridge (docs/addendum-designs/T1-v2-only-ctransaction.md)
changes how legacy transactions are named and how their coins are
recorded. t1_baseline_tests pins the values those changes must keep or
deliberately change:

- the regtest genesis hash and merkle root, which must stay identical;
- the TxId and TxHash of a pure v7 transaction, which must stay
  identical;
- the eCash serialization of a version 2 P2PKH spend and its SHA256d,
  which becomes that transaction's TxId and TxHash;
- the V2 state encoding of a legacy coin (the 0x80 form);
- the coins-database serialization of a legacy coin.

Later commits change these values only where the plan says so.

Rebase onto coordinator 276 (81e8ef1774): the two coin goldens
(legacy_state_coin_encoding, coin_serialization) take this stack's coin
record, which carries the coin provenance trailer and the coins-database
format magic.

Tier: V2

Coordinator integration provenance (network403):
Resolve integration context by retaining the incoming purposeful change together with existing shared/native consumers; exact old/new patch and file inventory is retained in owner-adaptations.json. No authored purpose or removed downstream behavior restored.
Original scripted commands/hashes above are original-author provenance; modified parent/tool/catalog hashes are not claimed to reproduce this composition. Exact coordinator adaptation scripts and ordered tree proof are in composed403-network-metrics-delivery. Build/runtime/benchmarks NOT_RUN for this composition under user compile-first policy.
